{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"1f013f6426b27f8cb555c22229b6c039f0c3bf25e128f377b49ae37cdbaeeacb","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira reconcile-bridge comment sync","key_entities":["REB-1861","REB-1580","REB-1829","comment_ids","RECONCILER_MARKER","_normalize_comment_body","_TRUNCATION_SUFFIX","outbound_comments.py","adapters/jira/comment_limits.py","712020:6471376f-4e5e-4ed2-8c05-330827bc387e","32403944666","reconcile-bridge.yml"],"problem_keywords":["duplicate comments","jira reconciliation","data cleanup","comment deduplication","bot-authored comments","outbound comment sync"],"propositions":["The outbound comment sync repeatedly re-posted the same comments to Jira on every hourly pass because the PRIMARY id-identity dedup skip comment_ids was inert/empty, causing 30,847 bot-authored duplicate comments across 30 issues and pinning REB-1861 at Jira's 5000-comment hard cap.","29,931 duplicate comments were safely deleted across 27 issues using a keep-oldest-per-distinct-normalized-body rule with pre-deletion backups, completeness gating, dry-run verification, canary execution, and post-deletion independent verification confirming zero missing bodies and unchanged non-candidate counts.","836 comments across three issues (REB-1567, REB-1931, REB-2605) carry no reconciler marker because outbound truncation at 32767 chars cut the marker paragraph off, and were deliberately excluded from phase-1 deletion pending an operator decision under --include-truncated.","The reconcile-bridge workflow remained paused throughout the cleanup operation and was not re-enabled, so the duplicate set is fixed and no longer growing.","Rate-limiting on 29,931+ DELETE operations was handled with explicit Retry-After backoff and 429 retry logic separate from transient-fault budgets, absorbing 713+ throttles with zero failed deletions.","REB-1861 comment count reduced from 5000 to 79; all 30 affected issues now hold exactly one copy of each distinct normalized body and are far below the 5000-comment cap."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787800427025926001,"uuid":"e8470c62-0747-4153-9297-da4090c4c403"}